{
  "id": "cauchy_number",
  "title": "Cauchy Number",
  "description": "Analyze fluid flow dynamics by calculating the Cauchy Number, a dimensionless value representing the ratio between inertial force and compressibility force in a flow.",
  "type": "chart-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Cauchy Number Calculator\n\nThe Cauchy Number is a dimensionless value useful for analyzing fluid flow dynamics problems where compressibility is a significant factor.\n\n### Formula\n\n**C = ρ v² / E**\n\nWhere:\n- **C** = Cauchy Number\n- **ρ** = Fluid density (kg/m³)\n- **v** = Flow velocity (m/s)\n- **E** = Bulk modulus of elasticity (N/m²)\n\n### Relationship to Mach Number\n\nThe Cauchy Number is the square of the Mach Number:\n\n**M² = C**\n\nWhere **M** = Mach Number"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "density",
          "label": "Fluid Density (ρ)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "kg/m³",
          "defaultValue": 1000
        },
        {
          "id": "velocity",
          "label": "Flow Velocity (v)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m/s",
          "defaultValue": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "bulk_modulus",
          "label": "Bulk Modulus of Elasticity (E)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "N/m²",
          "defaultValue": 2200000000
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "cauchy_number_result",
          "label": "Cauchy Number (C)",
          "formula": "inputs.density * inputs.velocity * inputs.velocity / inputs.bulk_modulus",
          "format": "scientific"
        },
        {
          "id": "mach_number",
          "label": "Mach Number (M)",
          "formula": "Math.sqrt(inputs.density * inputs.velocity * inputs.velocity / inputs.bulk_modulus)",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Density (kg/m³)",
        "Velocity (m/s)",
        "Bulk Modulus (N/m²)",
        "Cauchy Number",
        "Mach Number"
      ],
